{{ categoryHeading("Factory &amp; Credibility", "faq-credibility") }}
<div class="space-y-1">
{% call faqItem("Is WOWOHCOOL a real factory?") %}<p>Yes. WOWOHCOOL (Dong Yi Technology Co., Ltd) operates a 5,000m² ISO 9001 certified facility in Shenzhen since 2013. 200-500 staff including 50+ R&D engineers. 1M+ units monthly production capacity. Automated SMT lines and professional testing labs. Factory video tours and on-site visits welcome, <a href="/about/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline font-bold">learn more about our factory</a>.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("How is WOWOHCOOL different from a trading company?") %}<p>We own and operate our manufacturing facility, not a middleman. Real factory credentials: ISO 9001 certified since 2013, 5,000m² facility, 200-500 employees, 50+ R&D engineers, automated SMT production lines, and an in-house testing lab. Trading companies cannot offer the same level of quality control, pricing transparency, or production flexibility. We welcome video calls and on-site factory audits to verify.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("Can I visit your factory or do a video audit?") %}<p>Yes. We welcome on-site factory visits in Shenzhen, schedule in advance and we'll arrange a full tour of production lines, testing labs, and R&D center. For remote verification, we offer live video audits: walk through the facility via video call in real time. No appointment needed for video audits. <a href="/contact/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline font-bold">Contact us to arrange a visit</a>.</p>{% endcall %}
</div>
</div>

<div class="mb-16 reveal">
{{ categoryHeading("OEM/ODM Process", "faq-oem-odm") }}
<div class="space-y-1">
{% call faqItem("What is the difference between OEM and ODM?") %}<p>ODM: You select an existing product design from our platform and add your logo, colors, and stock packaging customization. MOQ from 500 units, lead time 25-30 days after sample approval. ODM new development (not in stock): 1,000-2,000 units, lead time 45-60 days — our 50+ R&D engineers handle the full development cycle. OEM: we manufacture your own design with new tooling, MOQ from 3,000 units. <a href="/service/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline font-bold">Explore our OEM/ODM services</a>.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("What is the step-by-step OEM process?") %}<p>1. Inquiry &amp; product selection, choose from 30+ existing SKUs across power banks, GaN chargers, wireless chargers, and car chargers. 2. Quotation within 24 hours, samples in 3-7 days. 3. Customization, your logo, packaging, and any minor modifications. 4. Sample approval, sign off on appearance and function. 5. Mass production, 25-30 days with 4-stage QC throughout. 6. Shipping, FOB Shenzhen, EXW, or DDP to your door.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("What is the typical ODM development timeline?") %}<p>ODM projects require 45-60 days from design approval to first shipment. Breakdown: Design &amp; engineering (7-14 days), prototyping &amp; tooling (14-21 days), certification testing (10-14 days), sample approval (3-7 days), mass production (25-30 days). Complex projects with unique tooling or new certifications may require additional time.</p>{% endcall %}
</div>
</div>

<div class="mb-16 reveal">
{{ categoryHeading("MOQ &amp; Pricing", "faq-moq") }}
<div class="space-y-1">
{% call faqItem("What is your minimum order quantity?") %}<p>MOQ starts at 500 units for ODM on in-stock models (logo + packaging customization). ODM new development (not in stock): 1,000-2,000 units. OEM with new tooling and custom engineering: 3,000+ units. Sample orders from 1-50 units for evaluation. Volume discounts available at 1,000+, 5,000+, and 10,000+ tiers.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("What are your payment terms?") %}<p>Standard terms: 30% deposit to start production, 70% balance before shipment. We accept T/T (wire transfer), L/C (Letter of Credit), PayPal, and Alibaba Trade Assurance. For established long-term partners, more flexible terms may be available. All payments secured through verified business accounts.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("What is included in your pricing?") %}<p>Unit pricing includes: product manufacturing, 4-stage QC testing, 4-hour aging test on every unit, CE/FCC/RoHS certification documentation, and standard packaging. Additional costs: custom tooling and molds, custom packaging design, regional certifications (UL, PSE, KC, SAA), special labeling, and express shipping. Request a detailed quotation for your specific requirements.</p>{% endcall %}
</div>
</div>

<div class="mb-16 reveal">
{{ categoryHeading("Customization &amp; Branding", "faq-branding") }}
<div class="space-y-1">
{% call faqItem("Can I put my logo on the products?") %}<p>Yes. Multiple branding methods available: laser engraving (most durable), silk screen printing, UV printing, or adhesive labels. Custom packaging with your brand design, instruction manuals, and inserts also available. Provide your logo in vector format (AI, EPS, or CDR) for best results. MOQ from 500 units for branded products.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("What packaging options are available?") %}<p>Standard: retail-ready color box or blister pack with your brand design. Premium: magnetic flap box, window display box, or eco-friendly kraft packaging. Bulk: plain brown box for distributors or Amazon FBA prep. Custom inserts, foam padding, and accessory compartments available. We assist with packaging design and provide mockups for approval before mass production.</p>{% endcall %}
</div>
</div>

<div class="mb-16 reveal">
{{ categoryHeading("Quality Control", "faq-quality") }}
<div class="space-y-1">
{% call faqItem("How can I check quality before mass production?") %}<p>Order samples first. Sample turnaround: 3-7 days for standard models. Check logo quality, workmanship, charging performance, and compatibility. Only approve samples after thorough testing. During mass production, our 4-stage QC process ensures consistent quality: IQC (incoming component inspection), IPQC (in-process monitoring), FQC (final functional test), OQC (outgoing quality check). 100% of units pass a 4-hour aging test before shipping.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("What is your 4-stage QC process?") %}<p>Stage 1, IQC (Incoming Quality Control): All raw materials and components inspected before entering production. Stage 2, IPQC (In-Process Quality Control): Real-time monitoring during SMT assembly, soldering, and assembly. Stage 3, FQC (Final Quality Control): 100% functional testing of every unit, charging speed, port output, safety protection, and compatibility. Stage 4, OQC (Outgoing Quality Control): Final appearance check, packaging verification, and quantity confirmation before shipping.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("What is your warranty and defect policy?") %}<p>Standard 12-month warranty on all OEM/ODM products, extendable to 24 months for qualified partners. Defect rate target: under 1%. For confirmed manufacturing defects, we provide replacement units or credit on your next order within 15 business days. Our after-sales team responds to quality issues within 24 hours. Long-term partners receive priority RMA processing.</p>{% endcall %}
</div>
</div>

<div class="mb-16 reveal">
{{ categoryHeading("Certifications", "faq-certifications") }}
<div class="space-y-1">
{% call faqItem("What certifications do I need for the EU market?") %}<p>Required: CE marking (electrical safety + EMC), RoHS (hazardous substances), WEEE registration. For products with lithium batteries: UN38.3 (transport safety) and battery directive compliance. Our products come with CE and RoHS documentation by default. We assist with obtaining additional certifications for your target EU markets.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("What certifications do I need for the US market?") %}<p>Required: FCC (electromagnetic interference), UL 62368-1 (safety standard for power supplies). Recommended: ETL or cUL for retail distribution. For power banks: UN38.3 for battery transport compliance. We provide FCC testing documentation with every OEM order and can coordinate UL/ETL certification through our partner testing labs. Certification lead time: 2-4 weeks.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("Do you help with the certification process?") %}<p>Yes. We handle certifications as part of our OEM/ODM service. Standard certifications (CE, FCC, RoHS, UN38.3) are included with every order. For market-specific certifications (UL for US, PSE for Japan, KC for Korea, SAA for Australia), we coordinate with accredited third-party labs and manage the application process. Certification costs are quoted separately for project-specific requirements.</p>{% endcall %}
</div>
</div>

<div class="mb-16 reveal">
{{ categoryHeading("Shipping &amp; Logistics", "faq-shipping") }}
<div class="space-y-1">
{% call faqItem("What shipping methods do you offer?") %}<p>Express (DHL, FedEx, UPS): 5-7 business days, best for samples and urgent small orders. Air freight: 7-14 business days, best for mid-sized orders (500-2,000 units). Sea freight: 25-35 business days, most economical for full container loads (5,000+ units). Shipping terms: FOB Shenzhen, EXW, CIF, or DDP door-to-door with all duties included.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("Can you ship to my Amazon FBA warehouse?") %}<p>Yes. We offer Amazon FBA-compliant fulfillment, including barcode labeling (FNSKU), poly bagging, case packing, pallet labeling, and shipping documentation. We work with Amazon-preferred carriers and have experience shipping FBA to US, UK, Germany, France, Italy, Spain, and Japan fulfillment centers. DDP shipping available for clear total landed cost.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("What is DDP shipping and is it right for me?") %}<p>DDP (Delivered Duty Paid) means we handle everything: export customs, freight, import customs, duty payment, and final delivery to your door, one price, no surprises. Recommended for first-time importers who want a hassle-free experience. Price is higher than FOB or EXW, but you avoid unexpected customs fees, delays, and paperwork.</p>{% endcall %}
</div>
</div>

<div class="mb-16 reveal">
{{ categoryHeading("Product Technology", "faq-technology") }}
<div class="space-y-1">
{% call faqItem("What is GaN technology and why does it matter?") %}<p>GaN (Gallium Nitride) is a semiconductor material that replaces traditional silicon in chargers. Benefits: 40% smaller size, 30% better heat dissipation, higher efficiency (less energy wasted as heat), and support for higher power output in compact form factors. WOWOHCOOL uses 5th generation GaN (GaN V) in our latest charger lines. <a href="/products/gan-charger/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline font-bold">Browse our GaN charger lineup</a>.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("What is a semi-solid-state battery?") %}<p>Semi-solid-state battery technology replaces the liquid electrolyte in traditional lithium-ion batteries with a gel-like solid electrolyte. Benefits: 50% thinner profile, 30% higher energy density, significantly reduced fire risk, and longer cycle life (500+ cycles). WOWOHCOOL's semi-solid-state power bank line was featured at CES 2026. <a href="/products/power-bank/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline font-bold">Explore semi-solid-state power banks</a>.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("What is Qi2 wireless charging?") %}<p>Qi2 is the latest wireless charging standard from the Wireless Power Consortium. Key feature: MPP (Magnetic Power Profile) uses N52H neodymium magnets for perfect alignment every time, ensuring 15W fast charging without the "searching for the sweet spot" frustration. Fully backwards compatible with existing Qi devices. Supports iPhone MagSafe and Android devices. <a href="/products/wireless-charger/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline font-bold">View Qi2 wireless chargers</a>.</p>{% endcall %}
</div>
</div>

<div class="mb-16 reveal">
{{ categoryHeading("Business Operations", "faq-operations") }}
<div class="space-y-1">
{% call faqItem("How do you protect my product design and IP?") %}<p>We take IP protection seriously. We sign NDAs and NNN (Non-Use, Non-Disclosure, Non-Circumvention) agreements. For OEM clients: your design files and specifications remain your property. For ODM: mutually agreed IP ownership terms in the contract. Molds and tooling owned by you remain under your control. We do not share client designs with third parties. For critical IP, we recommend design patent registration in China as additional protection.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("How does Chinese New Year affect production schedules?") %}<p>Chinese New Year (CNY) typically falls in January or February. Production closes for 10-14 days. We recommend placing orders 6-8 weeks before CNY to ensure production completion before the holiday. Post-CNY, production ramps up over 1-2 weeks. Q1 capacity is tight as factories fulfill pre-CNY backlog. We monitor the official CNY schedule annually and advise clients in advance.</p>{% endcall %}
{% call faqItem("How quickly do you respond to inquiries?") %}<p>We respond to all inquiries within 24 hours during business days, typically within 4 hours. Quotations provided within 24 hours of receiving your requirements. Samples ship within 3-7 days of order confirmation. Our team is available by email, phone, and WhatsApp. <a href="/contact/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline font-bold">Send us your inquiry</a>.</p>{% endcall %}
</div>
</div>

</div>
